  "content": "In a report released this week, Arctic Wolf described Kali365 as evolving from a purely Microsoft-focused phishing kit to a broader account-compromise platform that targets digital identities across AWS, Okta, Xerox DocuShare, and several Russian online services. The most notable among them is MAX Messenger, a Russian state-backed messaging platform with more than 80 million users that the Russian government has promoted as the country's national message service.",
